      "writtenOn": "2023-06-30T22:50:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Generally, we should try to use \"[positive boolean](http://shortn/_ZOoZV7ss2F)\"s for readability (i.e., not `CONFIG_DISABLE_UNALIGNED_ACCESS_TRAP`).\n\nTo avoid the ambiguity with `CONFIG_UNALIGNED_ACCESS` (is it allowed or not when enabled?), we could use either:\n\n* `CONFIG_TRAP_UNALIGNED_ACCESS` (symmetry with the [`TRAP_UNALIGNED_ACCESS` in our Zephyr implementation](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/Kconfig.defaults-arm;l\u003d7-8;drc\u003de113586363a26755dbd171b4b2d24aacc302780e))\n* `CONFIG_ALLOW_UNALIGNED_ACCESS`",
      "parentUuid": "a6c3ea47_aaf48c57",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "9cc6bdf7c41851685604b8289426bd95536904e5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
